 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send web push notifications to phones and desktops when something lands in someone's notification tray.
+To enable this, you need to provide a VAPID key pair.
+
+You can generate one with the web-push gem:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:latest bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then set both variables on your container:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` - the public key, shared with browsers when they subscribe
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` - the private key, used to sign push requests
+
+Once set, people can turn on push notifications for each of their devices from their notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
